Pricing models used in Booking, Expedia and Airbnb
You should choose the pricing model when you associate your property with Zodomus.
The pricing model used must be the same used in the channel, otherwise you can't send rates to the channel.
If the property is new use the recommended price model.
Check with your channel what is the current pricing model you are using now.

Zodomus uses the following price models:

Maximum / Single (only used in Booking)
In this price model you specify a default price for when the maximum number of adult guests stay in the room and a price for when a single adult guest stays in the room.
For single rooms, where single occupancy and maximum occupancy are the same, you only specify a price for maximum occupancy.
The optional restritions are parameters that you can use to set specific weekdays or specific restritions.
Some restritions may apply only to some channels, check with our support team for more information.

Code example:
                                        
                    POST /rates

                    JSON Body (For single rooms)
                    {
                      "channelId": "1",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "prices": {
                          "price":"100"
                      }
                    }

                    JSON Body (For non single rooms)
                    {
                      "channelId": "1",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "prices": {
                        "price":"100",
                        "priceSingle":"90",
                      }
                    }                    

                    Restritions: Optional parameters that can be included in the Json Body
                      "closed": "0=No" or "1=Yes"
                      "minAdvanceRes": Examples: 4D = four days; 4D4H = four days and four hours.
                      "maxAdvanceRes": Examples: 4D = four days; 4D4H = four days and four hours.
                      "minimumStay": Max. value: 31. Value must be less than maximum_stay and maximum_stay_arrival
                      "minimumStayArrival": Max.value: 31. Value must be less than maximum_stay and maximum_stay_arrival.
                      "maximumStay": Max.value: 31. Value must be greater than minimum_stay and minimum_stay_arrival
                      "maximumStayArrival": Max.value: 31. Value must be greater than minimum_stay and minimum_stay_arrival
                      "exactStayArrival": Max.value: 31.
                      "closedOnArrival": "0=No" or "1=Yes"                                            
                      "closedOnDeparture": "0=No" or "1=Yes"                                                         
                      "weekDays": { if all true its not used
                        "sun": "true or false",
                        "mon": "true or false",
                        "tue": "true or false",
                        "wed": "true or false",
                        "thu": "true or false",
                        "fri": "true or false",
                        "sat": "true or false",                                                                                                                                                
                      }
                    
                    


Derived pricing model (recommended Booking pricing model, only used in Booking)
Under the derived pricing model, you specify a price for a standard number of occupants, and one or more "offsets" to derive prices for other numbers of occupants.
When the number of occupants is different than the standard number, we add or subtract the offset from the standard price. An offset can be a percentage or an amount.
With the derived pricing model, you set prices in two steps:
1- Specify prices using the Maximum / Single model, just using the default price,
2- Specify the base occupancy and offset prices with the derived pricing model

Code example:
                                        
                    POST /rates (1st call)

                    JSON Body (To set the default price)
                    {
                      "channelId": "1",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "prices": {
                          "price":"100"
                      }
                    }

                    // Notes: PriceSingle cannot be set on POST rates (on derived prices model), it must be set on the POST rates-derived API

                    Restritions: Optional parameters that can be included in the Json Body
                      "closed": "0=No" or "1=Yes"
                      "minAdvanceRes": Examples: 4D = four days; 4D4H = four days and four hours.
                      "maxAdvanceRes": Examples: 4D = four days; 4D4H = four days and four hours.
                      "minimumStay": Max. value: 31. Value must be less than maximum_stay and maximum_stay_arrival
                      "minimumStayArrival": Max.value: 31. Value must be less than maximum_stay and maximum_stay_arrival.
                      "maximumStay": Max.value: 31. Value must be greater than minimum_stay and minimum_stay_arrival
                      "maximumStayArrival": Max.value: 31. Value must be greater than minimum_stay and minimum_stay_arrival
                      "exactStayArrival": Max.value: 31.
                      "closedOnArrival": "0=No" or "1=Yes"                                            
                      "closedOnDeparture": "0=No" or "1=Yes"                                                         
                      "weekDays": { if all true its not used
                        "sun": "true or false",
                        "mon": "true or false",
                        "tue": "true or false",
                        "wed": "true or false",
                        "thu": "true or false",
                        "fri": "true or false",
                        "sat": "true or false",                                                                                                                                                
                      }                    


                    POST /rates-derived (2nd call)

                    JSON Body (To set the derived prices)
                    {
                      "channelId": "1",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "baseOccupancy":"2",
                      "occupancy": [
                        {
                          "persons":"1",
                          "percentage":"-25",
                          "round":"1"						
                        },
                        {
                          "persons":"3",
                          "additional":"10",
                          "round":"1"						
                        }
                      ]
                    }                    

                    // Notes: Dates and currency are not used on the derived prices
                    //        The number of persons ("persons") must not be higher then the room MaxPersons, otherwise you will get an error from the channel
                    
                    


Occupancy pricing model (Recommended in Expedia not used in Booking for now)
Occupancy pricing model based on number of travelers staying in the room. It is recommended to define a rate for each applicable occupancy
You should set a price for each number of guests your room supports.
On Expedia the price is different for each date (On Booking derived prices the price stays the same for all dates).
If the reservation exceeds the number of guests you set , the higher number of guests price will be used by the channel

Code example:
                                        
                    POST /rates

                    JSON Body 
                    {
                      "channelId": "2",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "prices": [
                        {
                            "guests":"1",
                            "price":"100"		
                          },
                          {
                            "guests":"2",
                            "price":"110"		
                          },
                          {
                            "guests":"3",
                            "price":"130"		
                          }		
                      ],
	                    "closed":"0",
	                    "minimumStay": "3",                      
	                    "maximumStay": "20"                                         
                    }

                    
                    


Per day / Length of Stay pricing model (Used in Expedia and Airbnb (Per day only on Airbnb). PerDay and Occupancy are recommended in Expedia)
The Per day is similar to the maximum price used by booking
Length-of-stay is not so common on Expedia now.
Under length-of-stay (LOS) model, you specify a room price for every possible combination of length of stay.
You should set a price for each number of days you allow.
If the reservation exceeds the number of days you set , the higher day price will be used by the channel

Code example (Per Day):
                                        
                    POST /rates

                    JSON Body (Per day)
                    {
                      "channelId": "2",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "baseOccupancy":"2",                      
                      "prices": 
                        {
                          "price":"100"                          
                        },
                        ,
	                    "closed":"0",
	                    "minimumStay": "3",
	                    "weekDays": {
		                    "sun": "false",
		                    "mon": "true",		
		                    "tue": "true",
		                    "wed": "true",
		                    "thu": "true",
		                    "fri": "true",
		                    "sat": "false"		
	                    }                        
                    }

                    
                    

Code example (Length of Stay):
                                        
                    POST /rates

                    JSON Body (Length of Stay)
                    {
                      "channelId": "2",
                      "propertyId": "999999",
                      "roomId" : "90001",
                      "dateFrom": "2019-03-01",
                      "dateTo": "2019-03-31",
                      "currencyCode":"EUR",
                      "rateId":"99001",
                      "baseOccupancy":"2",                      
                      "prices": [
                        {
                          "days":"1",
                          "price":"100"                          
                        },
                        {
                          "days":"2",
                          "price":"100"                          
                        },                        
                        {
                          "days":"3",
                          "price":"90"                          
                        }
                      ]
                    }

                    
                    

