Start using our API's
Zodomus API's are REST API's with JSON requests and responses.
On the API reference you can get a detailed reference for each API.

Our API endpoint is : https://api.zodomus.com

To connect to our API and for security reasons you should use HTTPS and TLS (>=1.2).
Zodomus uses Basic Authentication, with the API User and API Password keys provided in the backoffice.

Let's see some examples to call one simple API : https://api.zodomus.com/channels, to get a list of active channels.

curl:
                                        
                    curl -u api_key_password:api_key_password -i -H 'Accept:application/json' https://api.zodomus.com/channels
                    
                    
Guzzle (Http client for PHP):
                    
                      $credentials = base64_encode($api_key_user.":".$api_key_password);

                      $client = new GuzzleHttp\Client();

                      $url="https://api.zodomus.com/channels";

                      $response = $client->request('GET',$url, [

                       'headers' => [

                          'Authorization' => ['Basic '.$credentials],

                          'Content-type' => 'application/json; charset=UTF8'

                        ]

                      ]);
                      
                      
Python:
                                            
                      import requests

                      from requests.auth import HTTPBasicAuth

                      r = requests.post('https://api.zodomus.com/channels', auth=HTTPBasicAuth('user', 'pass'))
                      
                      
C#:
                                            
                      WebRequest req = WebRequest.Create(@"https://api.zodomus.com/channels");
                      req.Method = "GET";
                      req.Headers["Authorization"] = "Basic " + Convert.ToBase64String(Encoding.Default.GetBytes("api_key_user:api_key_password"));
                      HttpWebResponse resp = req.GetResponse() as HttpWebResponse;
                      
                      
Test data
During tests you will use a limited set of channels, properties, rooms, rates and reservations.
The following data is available for your tests:

channelId: 1 (only Booking and Expedia channels are available during tests for the moment)
propertyId: Any integer you define for tests

Important note: On test mode most of the responses have fixed values and don't depend on your request values. For instance GET /availability will return always the same data.
The purpose of the tests are to provide you a sample of the data you will get on production.

Recomended steps to use our API's in tests
The following steps show the recommended path to use our API's during tests.

1 - Create all necessary information and test API calls on your software
You should create a property, rooms, rates and test the call of our API's to send and receive information.
In production is very important that you are ready to send availability and rates, and receive reservations before connecting to the OTA's

2 - GET /channels
Get a list of available channels and test you authentication keys in an easy API.

3 - GET /price-model
Get a list of available price models to use in the property activation.

4 - POST /property-activation
(Please note that for Airbnb there are some extra steps to connect the Host. See details on the next paragraph.)
Activate your channel / property with Zodomus.
In production you should provide the property ID and price model used in the channel.

5 - GET /room-rates
Get room and rates id's so that you can map your rooms and rates with the ones from the channel.

6 - POST /property-check
Check if your property is in evaluation to be able to activate your rooms.In test mode this operation allows the property to change state and continue tests.

7 - POST /rooms-activation
Activate your rooms and rates with Zodomus.
This API is used to inform Zodomus which rooms will be maped to channel rooms.

8 - POST /property-check
Check again if your property is active to get rooms and rates. If all is ok you can continue your tests.

9 - POST /availability
Post your availability for all your rooms for a period of a year (recommended by the channels).
As soon as you receive confirmation from your channel that the channel manager association is ready you should send you new rates and availability.
After connection to a new channel manager the channel usally clears all future rates and availability.
You should interpret dateTo as "up to and not including". In other words, a request with dateFrom="2019-08-27" and dateTo="2019-09-02" will apply to all days from 27 August 2019 to 1 September 2019.

10 - POST /rates
Post your rates for all your rooms for a period of a year (recommended by the channels).
You should interpret dateTo as "up to and not including". In other words, a request with dateFrom="2019-08-27" and dateTo="2019-09-02" will apply to all days from 27 August 2019 to 1 September 2019.

11 - GET /reservations-summary
If necessary get a summary of already made reservations (future reservations).
This API can be used to populated your software with future reservations that were made before the channel association.
It's optional, just use it if you needed it.
The reservations information retrieved is usually very limited, they don't provide a complete reservation dataset.

12 - POST /reservations-createtest
Use this API in tests to simulate the creation of a new reservation.
If you have a webhook activated, Zodomus will call you webhook with reservation data, otherwise you can use get reservations-queue to get the list.

13 - GET /reservations-queue
Check if new reservations are available.
You will get a list (or none) of new, modified or cancelled reservations.
If you have a webhook activated Zodomus will call you webhook with reservation data

14 - GET /reservations
Get a specific reservation, from the reservations queue list.
After a reservation is retrieved, it will no longer be available, so you should store the information after retrieval.
If a reservation is modified or cancelled by the guest a modified reservation will be available at /reservations-queue.
Since all reservation information and rooms can be modified or cancelled you should update or erase the reservation and rooms information.

15 - GET /reservations-cc
Get credit card info from a reservation.
You need to replace the normal API Password with the API Password CC to access this API.
If you are not PCI DSS certified you should not store the credit card data in you system.


