How to get Reservation data
Depending on your API access type you can get reservation information:

Reservations by API Call
In this mode you should call GET reservations-queue to check if there are any new reservations in Zodomus.
Then you should read the reservation data using the "GET reservations and GET reservations-cc" APIs

Reservations by Webhook
In this mode Zodomus we will call your webhook URL each time we receive a reservation from the channels.
The Webhook URL must be HTTPS.
The Webhook key is a string defined by you that we will send you on each call so that you can validate who is calling your webhook.
The webhook call is a POST command with a JSON body.
Even with the webhook active you can still call GET reservations-queue.
The webhook url will be called 3 times until we get success, after those 3 calls we give up. So if you have problems in your servers you should call reservations-queue to double check.

Webhook JSON Body fields sent to your URL:
                                            
                      webhookKey (Your webhook key, you should validate if a call to your webhook has the correct key)
                      token (Not used for now, we send a token we create)
                      channelId (Integer)
                      propertyId (String)
                      reservationId (String, sent from the channel to identify the reservation)
                      reservationStatus (Integer 1=new, 2=modified, 3=cancelled)
                      
                      
A call to to your webhook is made for each reservation we receive.
After you get the POST you should read the reservation data using the "GET reservations and GET reservations-cc" APIs

